# 🟠 Level 3 – Linux Firewalls

A firewall controls incoming and outgoing network traffic according to defined rules.

---

## UFW (Ubuntu Firewall)

Check status:

```bash
sudo ufw status
```

Enable:

```bash
sudo ufw enable
```

Allow SSH:

```bash
sudo ufw allow ssh
```

Block a port:

```bash
sudo ufw deny 23
```

(Telnet is typically avoided because it is unencrypted.)

---

## iptables

A powerful packet filtering framework used on many Linux systems.

Example:

```bash
sudo iptables -L
```

Displays firewall rules.

---

## firewalld

Common on Red Hat–based systems.

Status:

```bash
sudo firewall-cmd --state
```

List allowed services:

```bash
sudo firewall-cmd --list-services
```

---

