# 🌍 Real-World Example

A Linux web server should expose only:

* HTTPS (443)
* SSH (22) for administrators

Unused services and ports should remain closed to reduce the attack surface.

---

# Linux Network Hardening Checklist

✔ Enable firewall.

✔ Disable unused services.

✔ Keep SSH updated.

✔ Use SSH key authentication.

✔ Restrict administrator access.

✔ Monitor network logs.

✔ Keep systems patched.

✔ Close unnecessary ports.

---

# 🧠 Common Beginner Mistakes

❌ Leaving every port open.

❌ Allowing remote root login.

❌ Using Telnet instead of SSH.

❌ Ignoring firewall rules.

❌ Not reviewing listening services.

